<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01784</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>32716ae5-960f-4ab8-884a-24c0209ced20</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="4c51a73a-19f7-4195-bc6b-73db7facf308" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a86be7e9-a521-420f-bc87-0699ce61b7bf" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="16">
    <problem>
      <para>Sketch or describe the figure in Step 4 and Step 15.
          
          <figure><media alt="Three steps of a growing pattern"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7af9c38ee51b4d3864f92f32f049e74eb31e64ad"/></media></figure></para>
      <para> How many small squares are in Step 4? </para>
        <para> Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Step 4 is a 4-by-4 array of squares with the lower-left corner square moved to the upper-right corner.
      </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.2 and 7.3.3. 
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1efcfb52-3163-409c-870a-e78eba258ba3" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="225">
    <problem>
      <para> How many small squares are in Step 15?</para>
        <para> Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Step 15 is a 15-by-15 array of squares with the lower-left corner square moved to the upper-right corner.
      </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.2 and 7.3.3. 
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="bae33e1e-93fa-45e0-80cf-05879f2e5c72" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=n^2\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=n^2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=n^2+1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=n^2-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=n^2-n\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Which equation represents the relationship between the step number, \(n\), and the number of small squares, \(y\), in each step?</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=n^2\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.2 and 7.3.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="75564220-9969-4f6b-8201-1514dbe3b2c4" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=x^2-4\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=x^2\\) &quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2-4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2-8\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Each figure is composed of large squares and small squares. The side length of the large square is \(x\). Choose the correct expression that represents the area, \(y\), of the shaded part of each figure.</para>
      <para> Figure A 
            
            <figure><media alt="Large square with 1 by 1 small squares removed from each corner."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6f4278bac2d8a892bcfce054c9da28e0ad241e1d"/></media></figure></para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=x^2-4\) The figure is an \(x\)-by-\(x\) square with 4 unit squares that aren’t shaded.
      </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.3.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f4885315-c632-49bd-8ced-821d528863a3" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=2x^2+8\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=x^2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=2x^2+8\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x^2+8\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=2x^2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Figure B
            
            <figure><media alt="2 large squares side by side. On the side of the right square, there are 2 small squares stacked vertically, each with dimensions 2 by 2."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/054192d3c001b09c3745696ad0c2632da9ef6b91"/></media></figure></para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=2x^2+8\). There are two squares that are \(x\) by \(x\), and there are smaller squares that are 4 units each added to the figure.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="00953db5-9afb-4be6-92c1-ef559312ee4d" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="35">
    <problem>
      <para>Use the sequence below to answer questions a and b.</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="DIAGRAM WITH 3 FIGURES, SHOWING STEPS 1 THROUGH 3. STEP 1 HAS A RECTANGLE WITH 1 ROW AND 2 COLUMNS. 1 SQUARE IS ADDED TO THE TOP RIGHT. STEP 2 HAS A RECTANGLE WITH 2 ROWS AND 3 COLUMNS. 2 SQUARES ARE ADDED TO THE TOP RIGHT. STEP 3 HAS A RECTANGLE WITH 3 ROWS AND 4 COLUMNS. 3 SQUARES ARE ADDED TO THE TOP RIGHT."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b4c3cb9433e614fd5a11d44143280aa228c70485"/></media></figure></para>
      <para> How many squares are in Step 5? </para>
        <para> Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Every step has one more row and column than the step number, and then one square is taken away.
      </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.3 and 7.3.4. 
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5fe140cf-4801-41b8-a65b-577282d9e5db" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((n+1)^2-1\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(n-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(n^2-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((n+1)^2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((n+1)^2-1\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Choose the correct expression that represents the area, \(y\), of the shaded part of each figure for \(n\) steps.</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((n+1)^2-1\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.3 and 7.3.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div></section>
</content>
